EXPERIMENT 02 — SERVICE IDENTITY AUTHORIZATION

Requirement:
Allow Order Service to access Payment Service.
Deny Inventory Service and unknown workloads.

Security model:
L4: ztunnel allows traffic from the Payment waypoint.
L7: waypoint authorizes the original Order Service identity.

Expected:
Order -> Payment: HTTP 200
Inventory -> Payment: HTTP 403
Unknown -> Payment: HTTP 403

Actual terminal evidence:

PHASE 4 — CORRECTED L4 AND WAYPOINT AUTHORIZATION
L4: only payment-waypoint may reach Payment
L7: only order-service may use payment-service

ACCESS CHECK — Current AuthorizationPolicy configuration

$ kubectl exec deployment/api-gateway -- HTTP GET http://order-service:8080/order
HTTP 200
{"service":"order-service","inventory":{"service":"inventory-service","available":true},"payment":{"service":"payment-service","status":"healthy"}}

$ kubectl exec deployment/order-service -- HTTP GET http://payment-service:8080/health
HTTP 200
{"service":"payment-service","status":"healthy"}

$ kubectl exec deployment/inventory-service -- HTTP GET http://payment-service:8080/health
HTTP 403
RBAC: access denied

$ kubectl exec deployment/unknown-client -- HTTP GET http://payment-service:8080/health
HTTP 403
RBAC: access denied
